# A labelled call runs the overload the checker selected, also when the
# overloads are another unit's, reached through `using` (kexhq/kex#740).
# spec/named_overload_arity.kex covers one file; across units, BEAM placed
# the labels by whichever overload the interface listed under the name, and
# `send("e", "p", from: "dir")` ran the four-parameter `send` with
# `headers` = None.

using Postage

main do
  IO.printLine(send("e", "p"))
  IO.printLine(send("e", "p", from: "dir"))
  IO.printLine(send("e", "p", from: "dir", headers: 7))
  IO.printLine(Postage.send("e", "p", from: "dir"))
end
